{"name":"Paradise","hex":"#def1ea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Paradise","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Heaven.","The Garden of Eden."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Paradise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paradise","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and folklore, paradise is a place of everlasting happiness, delight, and bliss. Paradisiacal notions are often laden with pastoral imagery, and may be cosmogonical, eschatological, or both, often contrasted with the miseries of human civilization: in paradise there is only peace, prosperity, and happiness. Paradise is a place of contentment, a land of luxury and fulfillment containing ever-lasting bliss and delight. Paradise is often described as a \"higher place\", the holiest place, in contrast to this world, or underworlds such as hell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Angelico%2C_giudizio_universale_01.jpg/330px-Angelico%2C_giudizio_universale_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise","wikidata":"Q3363340"},{"title":"Paradise (2025 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Paradise is an American post-apocalyptic political thriller television series created by Dan Fogelman and starring Sterling K. Brown, Julianne Nicholson, and James Marsden. It was released on Hulu in the United States on January 26, 2025. The series has received generally positive reviews from critics, with praise for its premise, writing, and performances. The series has been nominated for eleven Primetime Emmy Awards, including two nominations for Outstanding Drama Series and acting nominations for Brown, Nicholson, Marsden and Woodley."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise_(2025_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q126126253"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Gardens_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg/500px-Gardens_of_Ashurbanipal.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki